    "description": "User19October2026: add a little X on the right side of the browser search input when something is entered, to quickly clear the search. Duplicate searches clear search/clear query found no matching issue. Related focus/textselection2805/2820 and current423/2817 should be reused and preserved, not reopened or copied into an independent text system.\n\nUse a compact \u00d7/clear action inside the existing search field right side, visible/enabled only while committed search text is nonempty. Reserve consistent inner geometry so text/caret/neighboring controls do not jump or wrap when it appears/disappears; input text must not paint under the hit target. Shared Hex theme/hover and accessible clear-search label, practical pointer hit area at current compact widths. Empty field has no distracting active X.\n\nClick clears through the normal browser query-update path, updates results/scope using existing search rules, and retains/focuses the actual search input ready for immediate replacement typing. Do not reset chosen source/filter scope or inject CommandF's global-All behavior merely to clear text. Preserve actual input selection/caret, Unicode, IME/shared composition cancellation semantics and keyboard focus guards; a stale async search response must not repopulate cleared query. No synthetic Enter/import/audition or neighboring source selection from button event propagation.\n\nAcceptance actual rendered pointer tests empty\u2192typedquery showsX; clear\u2192empty hidesX+results reflect clearedquery; type immediately after clear works without another click; existing CommandF/autoselect/doubleclick/selection/IME behavior preserved. Input+X bounds are stable and nonoverlapping at narrow/wide browser widths; hover/click no layout flicker; clear does not change scope/filter/track/project or insert/audition samples. Proportional focused local UI tests then solemerger exact checks/review/merge. Ready for Review only actualmerge; no app/native/install/quit.\n\nExisting general implementation worker queues with other new UI followups after current310/455coherentcheckpoint; no new worker or concurrent browser writer. Supported canonicalintake/attach/sourceidentity before implementation; preserve423/460andmerged324/414/411 changes. Keep3ongoingworkers. No new search/cache/history owner or global widget rewrite.",
